Here's a complete Java program that takes an input array of strings and sorts them in alphabetical order using the bubble sort algorithm. The program is modular, readable, and includes error handling for invalid inputs.
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.List;
import java.util.Scanner;

class StringArray {
    private String[] array;

    public StringArray(String[] arr) {
        this.array = arr;
    }

    public void bubbleSort() {
        boolean swapped;
        int n = array.length;

        for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
            swapped = false;

            for (int j = 0; j < n - 1 - i; j++) {
                if (array[j].compareTo(array[j + 1]) > 0) {
                    String temp = array[j];
                    array[j] = array[j + 1];
                    array[j + 1] = temp;
                    swapped = true;
                }
            }

            if (!swapped) {
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    public String[] getArray() {
        return array;
    }
}

public class BubbleSortApp {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter the size of the array: ");
        int n = scanner.nextInt();

        if (n < 2) {
            System.out.println("The array size should be greater than or equal to 2.");
            return;
        }

        System.out.println("Enter the strings one by one:");
        List<String> inputStrings = new ArrayList<String>();
        while (n-- > 0) {
            String s = scanner.nextLine();
            inputStrings.add(s);
        }

        StringArray sortedArray = new StringArray(inputStrings.toArray(new String[0]));
        sortedArray.bubbleSort();

        System.out.println("Sorted array:");
        for (String str : sortedArray.getArray()) {
            System.out.print(str + " ");
        }
    }
}
```
This program first defines a `StringArray` class that stores the input array of strings and implements the bubble sort algorithm. The `main` method of the `BubbleSortApp` class handles user inputs, validates the array size, reads input strings, and sorts the array before printing the result.

